{"name":"Grasshopper Pie","hex":"#bcdabb","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"grasshopper pie","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A kind of mint and chocolate pie, served chilled.","Used other than figuratively or idiomatically: see grasshopper,‎ pie."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grasshopper_pie"}],"entries":[{"title":"Grasshopper pie","blocks":[{"text":"Grasshopper pie is a no-bake mint-flavored mousse pie with a chocolate crumb crust. Typically light green in color, it is associated with spring, and especially with Easter celebrations in the United States. The pie takes its name from the Grasshopper cocktail."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Grasshopper_pie_%2814105460720%29.jpg/330px-Grasshopper_pie_%2814105460720%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grasshopper_pie","wikidata":"Q100507578"},{"title":"Grasshopper","blocks":[{"text":"Grasshoppers are a group of insects belonging to the suborder Caelifera. They are amongst what are possibly the most ancient living groups of chewing herbivorous insects, dating back to the early Triassic, around 250 million years ago."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/American_Bird_Grasshopper.jpg/330px-American_Bird_Grasshopper.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grasshopper","wikidata":"Q18398431"},{"title":"Pie","blocks":[{"text":"A pie is a baked dish which is usually made of a pastry dough casing that contains a filling of various sweet or savoury ingredients. Sweet pies may be filled with fruit, nuts, fruit preserves, brown sugar, sweetened vegetables, or with thicker fillings based on eggs and dairy. Savoury pies may be filled with meat, eggs and cheese, or a mixture of meat and vegetables."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Top_down_view_of_peach_pie_%28722379748%29.jpg/330px-Top_down_view_of_peach_pie_%28722379748%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pie","wikidata":"Q13360264"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Fossil_grasshoppers_-_Royal_Ontario_Museum_-_DSC00013.JPG/500px-Fossil_grasshoppers_-_Royal_Ontario_Museum_-_DSC00013.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Fossil_grasshoppers_-_Royal_Ontario_Museum_-_DSC00013.JPG/1280px-Fossil_grasshoppers_-_Royal_Ontario_Museum_-_DSC00013.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Fossil_grasshoppers_-_Royal_Ontario_Museum_-_DSC00013.JPG/500px-Fossil_grasshoppers_-_Royal_Ontario_Museum_-_DSC00013.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fossil grasshoppers at the Royal Ontario Museum","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFossil_grasshoppers_-_Royal_Ontario_Museum_-_DSC00013.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Two_grasshoppers_utah.jpg/500px-Two_grasshoppers_utah.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Two_grasshoppers_utah.jpg/1280px-Two_grasshoppers_utah.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Two_grasshoppers_utah.jpg/500px-Two_grasshoppers_utah.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Two differential grasshoppers, with spines along the tibia of the hind legs","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATwo_grasshoppers_utah.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Heupferd_